course: dictionary
lesson: 14039
title: Words for big houses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mansion is a very large, grand house, usually owned by a rich person. You can often work out the meaning from the clues around it. «The Harrisons moved into a mansion with forty rooms and a huge garden.» Forty rooms and a huge garden tell you it is far bigger than an ordinary house.
explain: Read the words before and after the word to find more clues. «The old mansion at the end of the lane had a locked iron gate.» Old, locked and iron gate suggest a big house hidden behind walls and gates. To check your idea, swap in your meaning: a very large, grand house with a gate still makes sense.
explain: Stories often use mansions for rich families, villains or ghosts. «The haunted mansion creaked at midnight.» Haunted and midnight show that the house is spooky. In everyday talk, people sometimes joke «It's not a mansion» about a small home, because they mean it is nothing like a grand house.
explain: In the UK, Mansions can also be part of a building's name. «We walked past Victoria Mansions, a tall block of flats.» Here the word does not mean one big house. If you meet a word you are unsure of, read the sentence again, then check a dictionary.
fact: Mansion means a very large, grand house, usually belonging to a rich person.
fact: Mansion is a noun. Its plural is mansions.
fact: In the UK, Mansions in a name, such as «Victoria Mansions», can mean a block of flats.
fact: Useful phrases include a huge mansion, a haunted mansion and a country mansion.
fact: Context clues such as many rooms, big gardens and gates help you know that a mansion is much bigger than an ordinary house.
exercise: «The Harrisons moved into a mansion with forty rooms and a huge garden.» What is a mansion? | A type of car | *A very large, grand house | A tent for camping | A small flat above a shop
exercise: «The haunted mansion creaked at midnight.» Which word is a clue that the house is spooky? | mansion | midnight | at | *haunted
exercise: Ella sees a sign on a tall building: «Victoria Mansions». What might it be? | A farm with cows and sheep | A castle with a moat | A garden shed full of tools | *A block of flats
test: Jayden says: «The Smiths' mansion has its own swimming pool.» What kind of family probably owns a mansion? | *A rich family | Nobody, because mansions are always empty | A very poor family with one small room | A family of cats
test: Which phrase means a big, grand house out in the countryside? | a plastic toy house | *a country mansion | a tiny studio flat | a haunted mansion
exam: Which sentence uses mansion correctly? | I ate a mansion for my lunch today | Our mansion is one bedroom with a tiny kitchen | My pet hamster lives in a mansion of straw | *The old lady's home had forty rooms, a ballroom and a long driveway, so it was a mansion
